# Nougat OCR stub — lucid100-uhdr-plasmid-dna-topas-nbio

**Status:** Not performed. The paper (`artifacts/paper.pdf`, 2.0 MB, 15 pp, CC-BY 4.0)
is fully text-extractable via `pdftotext -layout`, yielding a 1116-line
`artifacts/paper.txt` that contains the complete Methods (§2), Table 1
(43 chemistry reactions), Table 2 (11 experimental comparators), and all
numeric content of §3.1 (SSB results) and §3.2 (DSB results).

**Why no Nougat pass:**
- The IOPscience PDF is a natively-typeset LaTeX render, not a scan. `pdftotext -layout`
  captures column structure, table cell alignment, superscripts (with the two flagged
  exceptions in `REPORT.md` §7 which are actual paper-side typos, not OCR artifacts),
  and equation labels.
- Every quantitative claim in the analytic replication (`scripts/smoke_scavenging_capacity.py`,
  `scripts/smoke_dsb_audit.py`, `scripts/chemistry_table1.csv`) was sourced from
  `artifacts/paper.txt`. No content was missing that would have required Nougat's
  math-aware OCR.
- Nougat's marginal value here would be improved LaTeX rendering of Eq. (3) and
  Eq. (4), which are already correctly transcribed manually in the analytic scripts.

**If Nougat is ever run on this paper:**

